  "summary": "Bomkai sari or Bomkai Saree is a handloom saree from Odisha, India.",
  "description": "Bomkai sari or Bomkai Saree is a handloom saree from Odisha, India. It is an origin of Bomkai village from Ganjam district, however later it is mainly produced by the Bhulia community of Subarnapur district. Bomkai is one of the identified Geographical Indications of India. Bomkai Sarees are popular items displayed at various fashion shows.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Odisha; registration 2012–13), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
